From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:31:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The bus controller's CPU and GPU ports at the input/output
 setting TrimUI's hardware runs with (1, from their boot0, which ours doesn't
 run): at 0 the display missed its reads under load and drew broken rows, 175
 DSI errors in 904 frames on a busy screen, none at 1. SUNXI_NSI is built in
 and applies what each port's node in the tree gives, which its #if 0 had left
 out; the Brick's tree keeps the nsi-controller with only the two selects, and
 make-dt.py takes a set.txt for values TrimUI's tree gets wrong for their own
 hardware (it says 0 for the CPU)

---
 arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig | 1 +
 drivers/bus/sunxi_nsi.c            | 8 +++++---
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig
index 1a1be5a13..be29beab5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig
@@ -108,6 +108,7 @@ CONFIG_UEVENT_HELPER_PATH="/sbin/hotplug"
 CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
 CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
 CONFIG_DMA_CMA=y
+CONFIG_SUNXI_NSI=y
 CONFIG_SUNXI_RFKILL=y
 CONFIG_NETDEVICES=y
 CONFIG_TUN=y
diff --git a/drivers/bus/sunxi_nsi.c b/drivers/bus/sunxi_nsi.c
index 909d3cf1c..5b9d3db1a 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/sunxi_nsi.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/sunxi_nsi.c
@@ -298,6 +298,7 @@ static int nsi_probe(void)
 	/* the purpose freq of MBUS is 400M, has been configied by boot */
 
 	for_each_available_child_of_node(np, child) {
+		unsigned int val;
 
 		for_each_ports(port) {
 			if (strcmp(child->name, get_name(port)))
@@ -306,8 +307,10 @@ static int nsi_probe(void)
 				break;
 		}
 
-#if 0
-		unsigned int val;
+		/* Only what a port's node gives: the Brick's tree sets just the
+		 * CPU and GPU ports' select, the 1 TrimUI's boot0 leaves there,
+		 * which our boot loader doesn't. At 0 the display misses reads
+		 * under load and draws broken rows. */
 		if (!of_property_read_u32(child, "mode", &val)) {
 			nsi_port_setmode(port, val);
 		}
@@ -318,7 +321,6 @@ static int nsi_probe(void)
 
 		if (!of_property_read_u32(child, "select", &val))
 			nsi_port_setio(port, val);
-#endif
 
 	}
 
